CLAUDE.md: light/dark discipline, SEO, performance budgets, verification workflow

Folds in the gaps the doc was leaving open. The major additions:

* Theme system: new "Light/dark discipline" subsection codifying the
  rule that every new component must render correctly in both modes.
  Names the trap (static brand tokens like text-accent don't flip; use
  semantic text-foreground for body text). This is the exact bug
  Lighthouse caught on the placeholder hero (Charcoal-on-near-black,
  1.57:1 contrast). Now load-bearing.
* SEO: new top-level section. LocalBusiness JSON-LD template with the
  exact fields needed for NAP consistency with Google Business
  Profile. Per-page schemas (Service on /services, FAQPage on /faq,
  BreadcrumbList everywhere). Title/description length rules. Internal
  linking strategy (Plainfield-first cross-links). Image SEO. robots.txt
  content. Pre-launch SEO checklist.
* Performance budgets: new top-level section. Core Web Vitals targets
  (LCP < 1.0s on hero, CLS < 0.05, INP < 200ms). Bundle budgets per
  slot. Image weight by slot with Sanity URL params. Font loading
  strategy (no preload tag since Vite hashes filenames). Hydration
  strategy table mapping every React island to client:* directive.
* Visual verification workflow: new top-level section. Codifies the
  feedback loop. Every UI change verified in both themes, both
  viewports, all interactive states, with screenshots via Playwright
  MCP. Lighthouse on changed pages before PR.
* Accessibility: added touch targets (44x44), focus traps in modals,
  screen reader pass guidance (NVDA/VoiceOver), form error UX
  patterns, animation discipline (durations, easing, what to animate).
* Error and empty states: new top-level section. 404, form failure,
  no-projects-yet, Sanity reference resolution, content-not-yet-seeded.
* Image guidelines for editors: subsection in Image handling covering
  what Staci needs to know when uploading (source size, format, color
  profile, alt text, filename, hotspot).
* Form spam protection: subsection covering Web3Forms honeypot,
  hCaptcha, and rate limiting.
* Privacy and analytics: new subsection in Deployment. Documents the
  zero-cookies stance. No GA/Pixel/etc. without consent banner.
* Working with Claude: strengthened the verification mandate.

About 350 net new lines. The doc is longer but more load-bearing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
